The xFusionCorp development team added updates to the project that is maintained under /opt/beta.git repo and cloned under /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/beta. 
Recently some changes were made on Git server that is hosted on Storage server in Stratos DC. 
The DevOps team added some new Git remotes, so we need to update remote on /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/beta repository as per details mentioned below:

a. In /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/beta repo add a new remote dev_beta and point it to /opt/xfusioncorp_beta.git repository.

b. There is a file /tmp/index.html on same server; copy this file to the repo and add/commit to master branch.

c. Finally push master branch to this new remote origin.

SOLUTION
On Storage Server (ststor01)
SSH into the Storage server and switch to root:

bash
ssh natasha@ststor01
sudo su -
Go to the cloned beta repository:

bash
cd /usr/src/kodekloudrepos/beta
Add the new remote dev_beta:

bash
git remote add dev_beta /opt/xfusioncorp_beta.git
If the remote already exists, update it instead:

bash
git remote set-url dev_beta /opt/xfusioncorp_beta.git
Ensure you are on the master branch:

bash
git checkout master
Copy /tmp/index.html into the repository:

bash
cp /tmp/index.html .
Add and commit the file on master:

bash
git add index.html
git commit -m "Add index.html"
If Git reports missing identity, configure it first:

bash
git config user.email "devops@example.com"
git config user.name "DevOps"
Then retry the commit.

Push master to the new remote dev_beta:

bash
git push dev_beta master
Verify remotes and push:

bash
git remote -v
git log --oneline -3
Expected remote entry:

text
dev_beta    /opt/xfusioncorp_beta.git (fetch)
dev_beta    /opt/xfusioncorp_beta.git (push)
This adds dev_beta pointing to /opt/xfusioncorp_beta.git, commits /tmp/index.html on master, and pushes master to the new remote.
